From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:18:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power/stats: Use mobile radio active time when the modem
 reports no RX/TX

MobileRadioPowerStatsProcessor charges data transfers only through the
RX and TX times in ModemActivityInfo. Some modems leave them at zero:
on a Redmi Note 13 5G (MediaTek MT6833) on 5G SA, downloading 77 MB and
uploading 32 MB in a minute each reported only idle and sleep time, so
mobile data was never charged to anyone. The legacy calculator fell back
to the mobile radio active time for such modems; the power stats
pipeline lost that.

Collect the mobile radio active time, which the network stack drives
from the cellular interfaces' idle timers, alongside the modem activity.
When a period has no RX or TX power, estimate it as that time, less the
call time that PhoneCallPowerStatsProcessor already charges, at
radio.active, and share it between apps by their packets. Stats recorded
before this have no active time and are estimated as before.

Measured on that phone, with the CPU held awake and Wi-Fi off, the
transfers drew 130 to 190 mA above idle; its power profile has
radio.active at 194 mA.

Change-Id: Ie7bdc39782af5ed0697e9df631055349421f4972
---
 .../server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java  |  6 ++++
 .../stats/MobileRadioPowerStatsCollector.java | 14 ++++++++
 .../format/MobileRadioPowerStatsLayout.java   | 16 +++++++++
 .../MobileRadioPowerStatsProcessor.java       | 34 +++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

